From 1f77a6b0a9575afa6b9b7efd28cd2fb702e77f4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:39:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0150: blueline brightness (DCS 0x51, bluebl) and CS40L20
 haptics (bluehaptic)

Brightness (iokit/Kernel/arm/BlueBacklight.cpp, bluebl=1 default): the
SW43408's SET_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS (0x51, two bytes big-endian, panel range
8..900 = 2.74..399.81 nits, crosshatch dsi-panel-sw43408-dsc-fhd-cmd.dtsi)
as a DSI0 command-FIFO long write (DT 0x39) with the pingpong's autorefresh
stopped and drained around it, on AppleCLCD's vsync workloop thread, at
most every 2 vsyncs, never while the display is off, never below
bluebl_min (default 32). Requests are only recorded, from AppleCLCD
setProperties (brightness / IODisplayParameters / nits keys) and, at
bluebl=2, an AppleARMBacklight service with backlight-control = true (what
CoreBrightness matches; experimental). IOMFB selectors 50/66/67/68 are
logged. bluebl_test=1: 100 -> 20 -> 100 % ramp from 5 s, each write logged.
Any failed write turns the DCS path off for the boot.

Haptics (bsd/dev/blueline_haptic.c, off by default): the production
vibrator is a Cirrus CS40L20 at 0x43 on qupv3_se5 (GPIO 85/86, reset 87;
dtbo entry 8), bit-banged as 0141's MAX1720x. bluehaptic=1 probes (reset
pulse, OTP boot, DEVID/REVID/OTPID) and puts the reset pin back;
bluehaptic=2 runs the A0 bring-up (errata, OTP trims, boost 1 uH/4 uF/
4.5 A, routing, MPU, cs40l20.wmfw + cs40l20.bin from the ADT
/blueline-haptic, DSP start, 2 s playback cap) and makes /dev/bluehaptic
("click N", "vibe MS" <= 1000, "stop"). bluehaptic_test=1: three 50 ms
buzzes; =2: every wavetable click. Register sequence from Linux
drivers/misc/cs40l2x.c (as hardware documentation; rewritten).
BBI2C_MAX_BUSES 2 -> 4.
